dxmt, d3d11: Decode BC textures on the CPU.

Apple's A-series GPUs have no BC formats. Uploads to a BC texture are
decoded with bcdec, to RGBA8 or, for BC1 with KITSUNE_BC_16BIT, 16 bits per
texel. Large BC textures lose their top mips (d3d11.mipClampBC,
d3d11.bcMaxDim) while the application keeps its own descriptor.

Decoding at upload and IsBCFormat follow Madeira's DXMT fork
(willfaust/dxmt bc6d4c7).
